From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Normalize alphanumcase input like the other conversion functions

The original 1.2.0 test_alphanumcase expects alphanumcase(None) == 'None'.
Passing None directly to re.sub raises TypeError; the other converters already
normalize inputs with str(). Preserve the original test and make this converter
follow that established contract. No tests are removed or changed.

Source: repository-authored against official release-associated commit
be60b723753d4796983729d49ef825826e0f882d. Underlying source license: MIT.
Upstream status: local packaging fix, not submitted upstream.
Removal: drop when a future verified stable release normalizes this input and
its unchanged original/default tests pass without the patch.

--- a/stringcase.py
+++ b/stringcase.py
@@ -245,3 +245,3 @@ def alphanumcase(string):
     """
     # return filter(str.isalnum, str(string))
-    return re.sub("\W+", "", string)
+    return re.sub("\W+", "", str(string))
